  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. The compiler statically schedules every instruction ahead of time, down to the cycle. 144 ICUs stream a fixed sequence into their columns — no dynamic scheduling, no caches, no branch prediction.",
      "focus": [
        "icu"
      ],
      "dot": "icu",
      "explode": 0.4,
      "stage": "instruction-fetch"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Weights, activations and the KV-cache already sit in on-chip MEM slices — 230 MB of SRAM split across 20 superlanes, with no HBM or DRAM round-trip.",
      "focus": [
        "mem-west",
        "mem-east"
      ],
      "dot": "mem-west",
      "drill": "mem-detail",
      "stage": "sram"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Zoomed in: each MEM slice is built from 20 superlane SRAM banks (~5.5 MB each) running in lockstep with the matrix and vector units beside them.",
      "focus": [
        "sram-bank"
      ],
      "dot": "sram-bank",
      "drill": "mem-detail",
      "stage": "sram-bank"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. The VXM (5,120 vector ALUs) issues a vector instruction; the resulting data stream heads west toward the MXM.",
      "focus": [
        "vxm"
      ],
      "dot": "vxm",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "vector-unit"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. En route it passes through the SXM (switch unit), which can permute, rotate or broadcast lanes on the fly without touching memory.",
      "focus": [
        "sxm-west"
      ],
      "dot": "sxm-west",
      "stage": "switch-unit"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. The MXM's 320×320 fused multiply-accumulate array streams the activation vector past stationary weights, one row per cycle.",
      "focus": [
        "mxm-west"
      ],
      "dot": "mxm-west",
      "drill": "mxm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Zoomed in: the array is built from 20 stacked superlane rows (16 lanes each), giving the chip's maximum vector length of 320 elements.",
      "focus": [
        "macc-array"
      ],
      "dot": "macc-array",
      "drill": "mxm-detail",
      "stage": "superlane"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Partial products accumulate deterministically every cycle — the compiler already knows exactly when each result is ready, so there's no stalling or scoreboarding.",
      "focus": [
        "mxm-accumulator"
      ],
      "dot": "mxm-accumulator",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Results stream back east through the mirrored SXM/MEM slices in the east hemisphere, ready for the next statically-scheduled instruction.",
      "focus": [
        "sxm-east",
        "mem-east"
      ],
      "dot": "mem-east",
      "stage": "writeback"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. For models too large for one chip, RealScale C2C links extend the same fixed-latency pipeline across chips wired in a 2D torus — the whole multi-chip system stays cycle-deterministic.",
      "focus": [
        "c2c-link-x"
      ],
      "dot": "c2c-link-x",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    }
  ],
